Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:00:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Another area's maps drawn with their own textures and props
 (SDK_PORT_3DS)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

From Route 209 by its gate, Hearthome City past the trees was white, its
houses missing (two photos of 2026-11-06). Each map's textures and props
are its area's (its map header's area data); the game loads the player's
area's. A map of another one is behind a gate on the DS's screen, but the
wider field sees past the gates: Hearthome's ground textures aren't in
Route 209's set, and its houses' models aren't Route 209's props.

A map (loaded, or beside the loaded ones) with textures not in the field's
set is now drawn from a copy bound to its own area's (Port_OtherAreaOf):
that area's map and prop texture sets are read, their texels put in
texture slots 2 and 3 of the port's own (the field's VRAM is slots 0 and 1,
256 KB, and in play has about 45 KB left; an area needs 80-90 KB), their
palettes in the field's palette VRAM; its props' models are read as
they're needed and bound to its prop textures (MapPropManager_PortModelIDs
gives them from a map's props part). Two areas kept (the one used longest
ago let go, with the copies bound to it; not one used this scene), let go
with the loaded maps. Only while the field's textures are in slots 0 and 1
(A and B); the scenery maps ("everywhere") and maps whose textures are all
the field's as before. The log says each: `[field] another area's textures
...` and `the map at matrix M ... drawn with its own area's textures and
props`.

On the PC from Route 209 (520,712, 516,706, 513,721, 505,706): Hearthome's
brown paving, its house, lamps and hedges, as from Hearthome itself, where
it was white. From Hearthome looking east nothing read. From Route 203's
east end (252,763, 258,763) Oreburgh City's ground in place of white. No
other area read at Jubilife (185,778), Veilstone (719,617, 687,632) or
Route 207 (317,712).

